WEBVTT

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:18.990
That's a Spectral Nemesis.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.080
Everyone, don't break formation!

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.290
And don't go near the castle!

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.420
Yes, sir!

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.750
Now, all together! Gysoni!

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.130
Gysoni!

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.300
<i>The city of the Knights-sorcerers:</i>

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.820
<i>Caislean Merlin.</i>

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.020
<i>This city is currently threatened 
by mysterious monsters</i>

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.140
<i>which appear all at once, 
instead of hating from an egg.</i>

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:53.370
<i>They are known as Spectral Nemesis.</i>

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.300
<i>This city,</i>

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.380
<i>where it is said that the secrets of magic
 have slept since ancient times,</i>

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:02.060
<i>is where Seth's new adventure begins.</i>

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:39.010
<b>Toward a New Adventure 
-Overture-</b>

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.430
<i>"Toward a New Adventure."</i>

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:45.740
<i>In the battle at Rumble Town,</i>

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.690
<i>Seth saved the citizens
 from the unjust rule of the Inquisition.</i>

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:54.570
<i>But, of course, this did not mean an end
 to all the fighting in the world.</i>

00:02:55.350 --> 00:03:00.360
<i>To solve the mysteries of Radiant, 
the cause of all the fighting,</i>

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:01.990
<i>Seth left on a journey.</i>

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:07.010
<i>This would also be the beginning 
of his journey to learn</i>

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:09.040
<i>the secrets he held within himself.</i>

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.500
Caislean Merlin, huh?

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:27.750
If I go to that old city, I bet 
I'll find information about Radiant.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:32.140
I'll drop in, find what I need,
 and hop right back out!

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:37.660
I haven't been back home in so long.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:41.510
You're back, are you?

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:42.940
Y-Yeah.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:50.410
Man, I was hiding in there for
 so long, I thought I'd suffocate!

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.020
Right, Jiji?

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.420
Y-Y-Y-Y-You guys?!

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.550
Heya! It's been a while, boy!

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:00.910
Ruffians!

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.650
Don't you go slugging my servants!

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.300
What?! Why?!

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.310
Jiji! For no reason!

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:15.600
Lady Alma told us not to
 let the villagers see us,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.810
so we were just hiding here quietly!

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:20.820
What a mean thing to do!

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.940
Aw, you poor thing.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:26.420
Will someone please tell me
 what's going on?!

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:31.820
Sorry we startled you like that, boy.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.390
No, seriously, what are you doing here?

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.580
Whoa, whoa! Before we fill you in...

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:41.140
Jiji! Appearance pattern number 12!

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.990
Bravery Duet!

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:50.350
Jiji! Number 12, not number 21!

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.340
You screwed it up again!

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:55.380
We're a laughingstock thanks to you!

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.230
Duet? What happened to the other two guys?

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:04.930
Ah... We got separated
 when we fled Artemis.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.240
I wonder what they're up to right now.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.980
You don't catch on too quick, do you?

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:15.490
These two are working for me now.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:19.250
Huh?! But these guys attacked the village!

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:22.860
And then they tried
 to steal treasure from Artemis!

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:23.890
I know.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.380
Then why?!

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.390
I can answer that.

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.750
After Jiji and I fled from Artemis,

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:35.410
we hid out on a deserted island

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:38.190
to give our wounds time to heal.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:41.490
But there were Nemesis there!

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:42.780
Oh, come on.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.590
We had lost our weapons,
 our brooms, even our pants.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.110
We were certain
 that was the end for us.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:53.870
But then Lady Alma made
 a gallant entrance and saved us!

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.550
You saved them, Alma?

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:59.020
I happened to be traveling 
that way for work.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:02.140
Shouldn't you hand them
 over to Artemis?

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:05.470
I tried to do that, at first.

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:07.720
I sent word, but no one
 came to collect them.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.810
So I thought...

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.870
If they'll behave themselves, 
I might as well let them be free.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:19.930
It felt wrong to take their lives
 just because they committed a few crimes.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:26.280
I see.
 So that's why you decided to help Alma.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.850
Heck no!
 We ran away like scared rabbits!

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.070
Huh?!

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:35.290
But then she unleashed
 her magic at full blast.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.830
I show no mercy to punks
 who bite the hand that feeds them.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:46.590
But that's not all.
 Then a Source Nemesis showed up!

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:50.010
We were defenseless,
 and Lady Alma protected us.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:53.850
She took that Nemesis on by herself and won!

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:57.850
In that moment, I had an epiphany.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:02.860
What I saw before me was the spirit 
that I had been searching for!

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:06.640
The embodiment of courage, 
self-sacrifice, and humility...

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:09.370
It was right there in front of me!

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:12.870
Lady Alma... no, Goddess Alma!

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.310
Th-That's why I cast everything aside!

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:21.210
A lot may have happened
 between Lady Alma and me, but...

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:28.750
Huh?!
 I didn't understand a word of that!

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.160
Bossman, go start preparing dinner.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.500
Right away!

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:38.580
Honestly...

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:43.290
You really have tamed those guys.

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:46.480
They're just doing whatever I tell them.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:51.700
If I decided to sell my organs, 
they might actually help me do it.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:56.370
I guess it might be better
for than than being in jail, though.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.310
Maybe so.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:01.250
In any case,
 they've sworn loyalty to me,

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.850
and they do the work of ten men.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:04.970
Huh...

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:07.090
No need to worry.

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:12.510
It's cute how they think of me
 as their new family.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.500
Speaking of family...

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:18.510
I met this weird guy in Rumble Town.

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:20.390
Weird guy?

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.900
He... said he was my older brother.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.460
Sounds fishy.

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:31.180
He showed up out of nowhere
 and told you he was your brother?

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:33.070
He had horns, too.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:37.310
The curse of growing horns 
isn't that uncommon.

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:40.040
But he looked so much like me!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.110
And I felt... something strange.

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:45.480
Like I had a bond with him.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.250
A bond?

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:51.490
Like... within my soul, 
or maybe my memories...

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:55.260
It felt like I knew him.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:08:58.830
Seth.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:02.510
When you were fighting in Rumble Town,

00:09:02.510 --> 00:09:04.340
as strange as it sounds,

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:08.470
even though I was far away, 
I sensed the same thing.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:09.690
I sensed malice.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:13.900
It was not a pleasant feeling.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:19.160
As you know,
 I have no memories of my past, either.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:24.160
Your face may have been wounded
 as I tried to protect you from him.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:28.400
What makes you think that?

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:33.050
You think you can trust someone
 who didn't show up after that?

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:38.290
Besides, there's a bad feeling
 brewing inside me.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:42.180
At the very least,
 I know there's nothing safe about him.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:44.680
Chop!

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:45.930
Ow!

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:48.150
Get it together, boy!

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:51.290
Don't be swayed by the 
claims of some weirdo!

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.740
It wasn't that! It just felt like—

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:57.800
That's what you call
 an overactive imagination!

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:00.340
Next time you want to tell a tale like that,
 take notes first.

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:01.830
B-But...

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.670
No "buts"!

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:07.330
Listen to me. A lot of things are
 going to happen from here on.

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:13.570
Don't let them confuse you. Believe only 
what you've seen, known, and learned.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:16.530
If you get careless, you'll die.
 Understand?

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:18.340
Y-Yeah...

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:21.630
Lady Alma! Dinner's ready!

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:25.390
Sheesh... I'm starving. 
Seth, let's eat.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:27.350
Sure! I'll be right there!

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:31.100
What do you think, boy? 
Looks tasty, right?

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:36.580
<i>His brother?
 I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:44.950
<b>[Bravery Duet] 
A man who once lost his courage
 recovered it when he saw the goddess fight.
 But he lost his pants.</b>

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:51.670
<b>Arcadian Mountains</b>

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:10.300
<i>It's been three days
 since I entered these mountains.</i>

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:13.420
<i>Why have I been called out here?</i>

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:18.790
<i>If they were punishing me 
for letting Konrad go free,</i>

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:21.950
<i>they would have sent me back
 to my own country.</i>

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:23.990
<i>Konrad...</i>

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:28.930
<i>He had dangerous ideas 
right from the start.</i>

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:31.860
<i>If I had stopped him then,</i>

00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:35.130
<i>could that terrible tragedy 
have been avoided?</i>

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.550
<b>15 Years Ago</b>

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:44.050
<b>Rumble Town</b>

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:50.180
Don't let your guard down! 
They may still be in hiding!

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:54.980
Those Nemesis deceived us
 and attacked innocent people!

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.000
Report, sir!

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:58.900
The Nemesis have fled to District 13!

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:00.930
That's perfect!

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:02.870
We'll round them all up at once!

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:05.740
Captain! Something's moving over there!

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:06.800
What?

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:10.520
Vice Captain,
 take a look with that Goat Eye of yours!

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:13.920
It's not "Goat Eye," Captain.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:17.590
Sorry about that. Dormouse Eye, was it?

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:19.180
Wrong again.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:20.710
Mushroom Eye!

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:23.210
That's even further off.

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:27.300
Oh, who cares?! What do you see 
with that Fool Eye of yours?!

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.820
It's "Lynx Eye," Captain.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:35.140
I see a soldier.

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:39.320
From his uniform, I would say
 he's an Inquisitor assigned to the prison.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.730
Fire!

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:41.720
What?

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:44.360
It's obviously a Nemesis in disguise!

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:47.590
Uh... Let's at least hear him out.

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:49.450
Hey! What's the matter?

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:53.040
Th-There's a revolt in District 13!

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:58.400
The terrorists are holding citizens hostage!

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:01.250
They plan to execute them one by one!

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:05.370
A revolt at a time like this? Why?!

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:08.460
There are malcontents lurking everywhere!

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.560
Even the Major...

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:14.310
Even Major Oxumare was among them!

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.940
Major Oxumare is...

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.090
It can't be.

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:20.320
No... It makes sense.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:25.320
I did hear a report that he was 
overly friendly with the immigrants.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:30.200
Yes, sir! He was in communication 
with sorcerer children!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:35.530
Captain, let my squad handle this.

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:38.210
We'll free the hostages
 and find out what's going—

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:40.460
You can't do that!

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:44.120
Why not, soldier?

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:47.220
I-It's too dangerous!

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:52.230
Because... they have the 
Nemesis on their side!

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:56.410
Th-The terrorists are using Nemesis to fight?!

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:57.750
Yes!

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:02.730
Oxumare and those sorcerer children
 made all this happen!

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:04.450
What?!

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:07.370
Send our men to District 13 at once!

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:08.490
Wait, Captain!

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:12.990
I can't believe that the terrorists
 can communicate with Nemesis—

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:18.500
The chains!

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.000
The island is going to tilt!

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.660
Captain!

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:25.410
We must destroy the last anchor-point
 on Northeast Street

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:28.430
and sink District 13 entirely!

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:29.930
You...

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:35.930
We can save Rumble Town
 by sacrificing a part of it!

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:38.940
Then we need to evacuate 
the citizens first!

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.700
There's no time for that!

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:43.170
Precisely, sir!

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:47.940
If we don't act now, we'll be
 unleashing Nemesis all over the island!

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:49.730
Captain, sir—

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:50.890
Enough!

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:55.110
Vice Captain, if I waste time 
listening to you, it'll be too late!

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:57.950
Shoot that damned chain at once!

00:14:57.950 --> 00:15:00.420
Cut District 13 loose!

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:30.310
<i>I was too late. In everything.</i>

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:33.600
<i>How will regretting it help?</i>

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:37.200
<i>The detestable, guilty one... is me.</i>

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.730
<i>A dead end...</i>

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:48.020
<i>Where did I take a wrong turn?</i>

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:49.140
Dragunov!

00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:12.330
I've heard before

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:16.740
that the holy land of the Inquisitors
 was hidden somewhere.

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:22.110
Am I to be executed here?

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:24.020
What an honor.

00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:43.430
Is that...
 the Father of the Inquisitors?

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:45.520
Indeed.

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:51.950
This is the oldest and most faithful sculpture
 known in his image.

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:57.780
Welcome to our holy land,
 Captain Dragunov.

00:16:58.190 --> 00:16:59.540
General!

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.650
I didn't know this place really existed.

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:05.730
That is for the best.

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:10.300
We cannot allow blasphemers 
to know of this place.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:13.090
Since the scandal at Rumble Town,

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:17.300
the Inquisition's authority has plummeted.

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:21.240
I took the risk of exposing 
Konrad's evil deeds,

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:24.570
because I couldn't allow myself 
to make the same mistake twice.

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:27.520
I had no desire to sully 
the honor of the Inquisition.

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:29.150
That is enough.

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:33.340
If I were going to rebuke you,

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:37.660
I would not do so here,
 but at our home base in Bome.

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:40.280
Rise.

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:42.230
I have no intention of punishing you.

00:17:44.860 --> 00:17:48.450
We face the onset of an era 
of unprecedented difficulty.

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:50.970
The scheming Domitors,

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.630
the Knights-sorcerers of Caislean Merlin,

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:58.180
the Merchant Baron's gang
 in the Ponantin countries...

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:02.090
However, none but the Inquisition 
are truly concerned about

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:04.180
the future of humanity.

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.550
We, the Thaumaturges,

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:09.560
are putting forth our utmost effort
 to correct this world.

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:14.820
At times, maintaining such a delicate balance
 requires decisive measures.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.070
That responsibility lies with me.

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:24.580
Therefore, Captain Dragunov,
 the one with jurisdiction over Pompo Hills...

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:26.020
is dead.

00:18:26.770 --> 00:18:30.220
You will be henceforth known
 as Captain Dragunov the Thaumaturge.

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:36.810
Your discerning eye was a 
double-edged sword in this incident.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:42.790
But without it, we would not have
 uncovered the truth of the matter.

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:45.350
I-I am unworthy of such praise.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:50.480
I only happened to be there
 as a spectator.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.250
Your humility is commendable.

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:55.610
Von Teppes was not like you.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:19:00.740
He overestimated his power and was defeated
 before he could use his miracle.

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:04.210
I recommended you.

00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:07.830
I once served under you, after all.

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:11.830
I'm very familiar with your observant eye
 and your dedication.

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:16.210
Having a man with your judgment
 among the Thaumaturges would give us

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:17.630
the strength of a hundred men.

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:21.090
<i>I was fully prepared to be executed.</i>

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:24.640
<i>I never imagined
I'd become a Thaumaturge.</i>

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:26.410
Come.

00:19:28.990 --> 00:19:32.810
The sorcerers with whom
 we Thaumaturges fight are powerful.

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:37.450
In ages past,

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:41.730
the people were ruled
 by tremendously powerful sorcerers.

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:43.770
But then, one day,

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:47.900
one man rose to fly the flag of rebellion
 against their oppression.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:51.700
That man, said to be the son
 of a simple farmer,

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:56.700
faced the sorcerers with his own will
 as his only weapon.

00:19:57.230 --> 00:20:00.630
Today, this is thought to be no more
 than a fairy tale,

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:03.760
but it is a true story.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:07.010
Is that... the Father's trident?

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:10.590
Yes. It is one of our sacred relics.

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:16.090
Not a magical implement, 
but a simple farm tool.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:21.400
How did our Father confront such 
supernatural power with a simple farm tool?

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:24.060
That truly is a miracle.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:25.950
Precisely.

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:29.570
He performed a miracle
 with only the power of his own will.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.540
What does that mean?

00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:34.460
I will tell you when the time is right.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:38.870
You must be exhausted after your journey.
 You should rest.

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:43.800
We will perform the ritual
 to declare you a Thaumaturge later.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:44.810
Yes, sir.

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:48.810
Tomorrow at dawn,
 you will depart with Liselotte.

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:52.310
This will be your first mission
 as a Thaumaturge.

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:56.700
You are to find that horned sorcerer
 and his companions.

00:20:58.390 --> 00:21:03.490
<i>The boy who challenged the Domitor 
and resolved the incident...</i>

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:07.290
<i>For the Inquisition to be so persistent
 about finding him...</i>

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:09.780
<i>Then there really is something behind it?</i>

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:18.460
You are the only one
 who has seen all their faces.

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:20.130
You can count on me.

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:24.130
I will never forget their faces.

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.970
Caislean Merlin...

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:34.830
Isn't that the ancient city
 where it's said that magic originated?

00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:39.750
If you ask me,
 he's just grasping at straws.

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:45.250
But some people called 
Knights-sorcerers run the show there.

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:48.160
For a guy like me,
 it's a pretty awkward place to be.

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:53.980
So, are you sure you won't
 go with him, Lady Alma?

00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:58.620
I'm not going.
 I have my own business to attend to.

00:21:58.620 --> 00:21:59.640
Yes, ma'am!

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:04.130
He made up his own mind
 to set out on this journey.

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:06.420
Is this what they call a parent's love?!

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:07.510
Like hell it is!

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:27.020
So that's... the continent of Cyfandir!

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:29.990
To Be Continued

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:01.020 --> 00:24:04.550
<i>Seth finally sets foot in Cyfandir alone.</i>

00:24:05.050 --> 00:24:08.470
<i>There, he immediately encounters 
the Merchant Baron,</i>

00:24:08.470 --> 00:24:11.830
<i>who wants the nation's resources 
for himself and his gang.</i>

00:24:12.350 --> 00:24:15.510
<i>After being chased by the unscrupulous 
Merchant Baron and his gang,</i>

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:18.770
<i>Seth runs into someone
 he hadn't expected to see again.</i>

00:24:19.290 --> 00:24:22.900
<i>Next time on <i>Radiant</i>, 
"An Encounter in the Rain."</i>

00:24:21.120 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>An Encounter in the Rain 
-Mist-</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>Did you see my gallant self?!</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
Your time in this story
 is over, Kon-kon.

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>End</b>
